WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.020
Film Courage: This is from viewer TJW “When
writing a TV spec, how far in the future should

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.400
you know your story, multiple seasons?”

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.941
Peter Russell, Screenwriter/Story Doctor:
I would say so.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:14.880
I think you should know what the ending is
going to be.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:20.880
What is interesting is you take a show like
MADMEN but you know that at the end of the

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.630
show nothing is going to be any different
than the beginning.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.680
It really isn’t.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:31.790
The first episode of MADMEN Don Draper is
a New York ad man who is really unhappy in

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:35.780
his marriage and he’s got a big hole in
his soul.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:42.030
What’s the last final scene with Don Draper.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.860
He is going to go back and be a New York ad
man.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:49.040
He is a seducer of women, he has a problem
with his relationship with women and he’s

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.399
got a big hole in his soul, right?

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:57.440
So it’s not hard to know the ending of your
TV show because it’s going to be the same

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.440
as your beginning.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:07.069
There really is no, unless it’s a miniseries
where like TRUE DETECTIVE where season one

00:01:07.069 --> 00:01:13.579
Rusty and Marty change incredibly because
that’s a movie basically (remember miniseries

00:01:13.579 --> 00:01:18.750
are long movies) you’re always just going
to be in the same place so yeah knowing the

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:19.750
ending is not hard.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:23.380
You’re going to be in exactly the same place
as you were in the beginning.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.090
BUFFY THE VAMPIRE SLAYER is still slaying
vampires is not happy about it.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:34.189
[Danny] Glover in ATLANTA for however long
ATLANTA it goes unless he just wants to say

00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:35.189
“Screw You!”

00:01:35.189 --> 00:01:38.320
I’m not going to do what you expect me to
do, his character is still going to be bumping

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.859
along feeling like a loser at the very end
of ATLANTA.

00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:44.149
SNEAKY PETE same thing.

00:01:44.149 --> 00:01:49.989
SNEAKY PETE is still going to be conflicted
by having a family versus being a con artist,

00:01:49.989 --> 00:01:51.759
being along versus being with his family.

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:54.060
I don’t care how many seasons you have.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:58.539
So it’s not hard figuring out where your
television show is going because it’s going

00:01:58.539 --> 00:01:59.999
nowhere.

